  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07): all 7 patients reviewed.\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg BID. Itraconazole course finished 8/14; no dose criteria met.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: rivaroxaban first cut 20 → 15 mg on SCr 160 µmol/L. St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL); CrCl 60 → back to 20 mg daily (mr-t0013). Correction note written.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg BID (taking itraconazole; no dose criteria met).\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: apixaban 5 mg BID correct (only age ≥80 met). ED creatinine that came in during the review (latest 100 µmol/L = 1.13 mg/dL) doesn't change this. No change.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 → 20 mg daily. CrCl 56 on actual weight 96 kg; the earlier cut used ideal weight. A home-scale weight of 185 lb arrived but is patient-reported, so not used; decision stands.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg daily. New SCr 1.25 (10/22, arrived during review); CrCl 43.6.\n- pt-0002 Vance: first raised 2.5 → 5 mg BID (only age met). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived: itraconazole started 10/22 for 12 weeks. Corrected back to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0014). Correction note written.\nEach change has a cited progress note. Itraconazole and all other drugs left unchanged. Inbox items for the 5 arrivals closed. pt-0041 and pt-0002 need apixaban re-reviewed when itraconazole ends.",
